# The Action's committed bundle is a build artifact, not text.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites its line
# endings on checkout, which makes `git diff --check` report trailing whitespace
# on three megabyte-long lines and makes `bun run check:dist` fail on a bundle
# that is byte-identical to the committed one. Git must not touch these bytes.
action/dist/** -text

# Everything `cargo xtask automation check` generates is compared byte for byte.
#
# That check proves the committed files are exactly what the Rust types produce,
# so a checkout that rewrites their line endings makes it fail on bytes nothing
# changed: a fresh Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true` turned them CRLF, and
# all sixteen files were reported as 28 to 63 bytes "longer" than what was
# generated. They are LF in the index and LF out of the generator, so marking them
# `-text` is what makes the comparison mean what it says on every platform.
schema/automation-v1.schema.json -text
action/src/protocol.generated.ts -text
fixtures/automation/** -text
